<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francisco Franco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1892–1975</span> · Also known as Generalísimo Franco</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francisco Franco was a Spanish general who rose in the colonial wars in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>. In July 1936 he led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armee-d-afrique">Army of Africa</a> in the military rising against the Second Republic and was named head of state of the Nationalist side. After winning the civil war in 1939 he ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> as dictator until his death in 1975.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francisco-franco.jpg" alt="Francisco Franco" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francisco_Franco_posed_portrait_photograph.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
